      "message": "Rather than trying to test all the various formats in a single test, I would try to break into smaller focused tests, which are easier to debug when they fail.\n\nFor example,\n\n```\nclass LsbvalTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    \"\"\"Test the correctness of the lsbval parser\"\"\"\n\n    @mock.patch(\u0027fptool.read_lsbval\u0027)\n    def test_lsbval_leading_and_trailing_spaces(self, mock_lsbval):\n        mock_lsbval.return_value \u003d [\n           \u0027        WS_KEY  \u003d    value       \u0027,\n        ]\n        ret \u003d fptool.lsbval(\u0027WS_KEY\u0027)\n        self.assertEqual(ret, \u0027value\u0027)\n\n    @mock.patch(\u0027fptool.read_lsbval\u0027)\n    def test_lsbval_double_quotes(self, mock_lsbval):\n        mock_lsbval.return_value \u003d [\n           \u0027DOUBLE_QUOTES \u003d \\\"double\\\"\u0027,\n        ]\n        ret \u003d fptool.lsbval(\u0027DOUBLE_QUOTES\u0027)\n        self.assertEqual(ret, \u0027\"double\"\u0027)\n\n\nclass PlatformNameTest(unittest.TestCase):\n\n    @mock.patch(\u0027fptool.read_lsbval\u0027)\n    def test_get_platform_name(self, mock_lsbval):\n        mock_lsbval.return_value \u003d [\n           \u0027CHROMEOS_RELEASE_BOARD\u003dzork\u0027,\n        ]\n        platform_name \u003d fptool.get_platform_name()\n        assert platform_name \u003d\u003d \u0027zork\u0027\n```",
